<tbody>
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="mob-pt-10 mob-ps-0" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 21px; padding-right: 20px; padding-bottom: 12px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 21px;">Tuesday 14th October</span></p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="mob-ps-0" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 14px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 21px; padding-right: 20px; padding-bottom: 16px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;">Following the Failure to Prevent Fraud Act released by ECCTA in September, join us at our community meeting where Bridget will be hosting a fireside chat with Helen Bennett from Cardiff University and Dan Harris from Kaplan about this new Act and what Institutions need to do.</span></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 21px;">We will also be hearing about some new research being undertaken by Professor Nic Ryder and his team, who previously published one of the few research papers focused on AML in Higher Education. Finally, as always there will be the opportunity for you to share your best practice and get advice from Flywire and your peers around Fraud and Money Laundering.</span></p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" style="padding-right: 20px; width: 100%;"> 
